# Lines tools/check-serial must see, in this order, as whole serial lines,
# for ui-demo on the Raspberry Pi 5 (systems/rpi5b_2gb/ui-demo.system):
# every line of systems/ui-demo.expect, in its order (tools/test_tools.py
# checks), and the display PD's lines for the board's framebuffer - where it
# shows each frame, and the hash of what the window holds once it has: the
# frame at the monitor's own pixels, 1920x1064 r5g6b5 from row 16,
# read back. crates/nowayos-demo/tests/frame_hash.rs computes each scan-out
# hash from the step's approved golden image. With a monitor at 1920 x 1080,
# the HVS's channel 0 scans it out, and copies wait for it.
NOWAYOS: display-stub: starting
NOWAYOS: display-stub: showing each frame on the board's 1920x1080 r5g6b5 framebuffer at its own pixels, from row 16
NOWAYOS: display-stub: copies keep in step with the scan, on display channel 0
NOWAYOS: display-stub: announced 1920x1064 Rgb565 at scale 2
NOWAYOS: input-script: starting; 10 steps to play
NOWAYOS: ui: starting
NOWAYOS: ui: the display is 1920x1064 Rgb565 at scale 2
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 0 hash 0xa1d7ff36f18a8b5e
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 0 on the framebuffer, scan-out hash 0xa1d7ff36f18a8b5e
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 1 hash 0xa1d7ff36f18a8b5e
NOWAYOS: display-stub: frame 1 on the framebuffer, scan-out hash 0xa1d7ff36f18a8b5e
